=>*
  (msg finishAsymEncrypt[^ CIPHERRESULT] from oid(101, testTa) to testTa)
  < oid(101, testTa) : OperationHandle | oid : oid(1, testTa),
      state : handleState(keySet), opclass : clsAsymmetricCipher >
  C .

--- DeriveKey links top-level operation and destination object handles.
search [1] in COMPLETION-TEST :
  (msg deriveKey[^ (empty).Set{CryptoAttribute} ^ oid(102, testTa)] from testTa to oid(101, testTa))
  < oid(1, testTa) : CryptoOperation |
      mode : modeDerive >
  < oid(101, testTa) : OperationHandle | oid : oid(1, testTa),
      state : handleState(keySet), opclass : clsKeyDerivation >
  < oid(2, testTa) : TransientObject |
      initialized : false, type : typeGenericSecret,
      attributes : empty >
  < oid(102, testTa) : ObjectHandle | oid : oid(2, testTa) >
=>*
  (msg finishDeriveKey[] from oid(102, testTa) to testTa)
  < oid(101, testTa) : OperationHandle | oid : oid(1, testTa),
      state : handleState(keySet), opclass : clsKeyDerivation >
  < oid(102, testTa) : ObjectHandle | oid : oid(2, testTa) >
  C .

--- Asymmetric capacity checks resolve the top-level operation owner.
search [1] in COMPLETION-TEST :
  < testTa : TAKernel | api-call : init(apiCall(AsymmetricEncrypt , (handle(oid(101, testTa)),
                                          data(randomData), capacity(dataSize(0))))) >
  < oid(1, testTa) : CryptoOperation |
      attributes : attr(rsaModulus, randomAttrVal),
      algorithm : algRsaesPkcs1OaepMgf1Sha1,
      max-size : 2048, mode : modeEncrypt >
  < oid(101, testTa) : OperationHandle | oid : oid(1, testTa),
      key-material-set : true, opclass : clsAsymmetricCipher >
=>*
  < testTa : TAKernel | api-call : return(apiCall(AsymmetricEncrypt , (retCode(errorShortBuffer) , size(dataSize(256))))) >
  < oid(1, testTa) : CryptoOperation |
      attributes : attr(rsaModulus, randomAttrVal),
      algorithm : algRsaesPkcs1OaepMgf1Sha1,
      max-size : 2048, mode : modeEncrypt >
  < oid(101, testTa) : OperationHandle | oid : oid(1, testTa),
      key-material-set : true, opclass : clsAsymmetricCipher > .

--- Asymmetric signing resolves a top-level key-set operation handle.
